# Imprint environment variable example
#
# The CLI (`imprint extract --intelligence ...`) and MCP (`imprint_interpret`) read these process variables.
#
# Notes:
# - Desktop AI settings live in the app's userData directory and do not conflict with this file.
# - Node does not load .env automatically. Set real process variables with setx/export or load a copied file yourself.
# - Process environment variables take precedence over variables loaded from this file.
# - Real .env files are ignored by Git. Never commit actual credentials.

# Global overrides take precedence over provider-specific keys. Custom providers also require IMPRINT_AI_BASE_URL.
# IMPRINT_AI_API_KEY=
# IMPRINT_AI_BASE_URL=
# IMPRINT_AI_MODEL=

# Standard provider keys used by the CLI and MCP server
# OPENAI_API_KEY=
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# ALIBABA_API_KEY=
# ZHIPU_API_KEY=
# XAI_API_KEY=

# Optional provider-specific overrides
# OPENAI_MODEL=
# OPENAI_BASE_URL=
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=
